# spiderlint findings for ORIGIN

## links/broken-internal (error)

http.status is 404; linked from 12 pages

Where: /missing, used by or shared with:
- /
- /about
- /app/
- /posts/1
- /posts/2
- /posts/3
- /posts/4
- /posts/5
- /tags/a
- /tags/b
- /tags/c
- /orphan
Reads: `http.status`, `crawl.referrers`
Fix: Fix the page at the link target so it answers 2xx, or point the links to a working URL.
Docs: https://developers.google.com/search/docs/crawling-indexing/http-network-errors
Done when: `spiderlint audit ORIGIN/ --rules links/broken-internal` reports no links/broken-internal finding.

## html/one-h1 (error)

should have exactly one <h1>, found none

Where: 5 pages of group posts (100 %), for example:
- /posts/1
- /posts/2
- /posts/3
Reads: `html.h1`, expects `{"type":"array","minItems":1,"maxItems":1}`
Fix: Use exactly one <h1> per page.
Docs: https://developer.mozilla.org/docs/Web/HTML/Reference/Elements/Heading_Elements
Done when: `spiderlint audit ORIGIN/ --rules html/one-h1` reports no html/one-h1 finding.

## html/viewport (warning)

meta viewport should set width=device-width and allow zoom, found none

Where: 8 pages of group default (100 %), for example:
- /
- /about
- /app/
Reads: `html.meta.viewport`, expects `{"type":"string","pattern":"^(?!.*(?i:user-scalable)\\s*=\\s*(?i:no|0)\\b)(?!.*(?i:maximum-scale)\\s*=\\s*1(\\.0+)?(?![\\d.]))(?=.*(?i:width\\s*=\\s*device-width))"}`
Fix: Set <meta name=viewport content="width=device-width"> and allow zoom.
Docs: https://developer.mozilla.org/docs/Web/HTML/Viewport_meta_tag
Done when: `spiderlint audit ORIGIN/ --rules html/viewport` reports no html/viewport finding.

