## html/description-redundant (warning)

meta description repeats itself around a separator: 51 characters: “Duplicate content notice - Duplicate content notice”

Where: /duplicate
Reads: `html.meta.description`, expects `{"type":"string","pattern":"^(?!.*(.{2,120}?)\\s*[-|:–—·»]\\s*\\1$).*$"}`
Fix: Remove the repeated suffix from the meta description.
Docs: https://developers.google.com/search/docs/appearance/snippet
Done when: `spiderlint audit ORIGIN/ --rules html/description-redundant` reports no html/description-redundant finding, and `spiderlint facts ORIGIN/duplicate` shows `html.meta.description` meeting it.

