## html/theme-color-schemes (warning)

color-scheme names light and dark, but no theme-color pair carries a prefers-color-scheme media

Where: /about
Reads: `html.metas`, expects `{"allOf":[{"contains":{"properties":{"name":{"const":"theme-color"}},"required":["name"]},"minContains":2},{"contains":{"properties":{"name":{"const":"theme-color"},"media":{"pattern":"(?i:prefers-color-scheme)"}},"required":["name","media"]}}]}`
Fix: Add <meta name=theme-color media="(prefers-color-scheme: dark)"> beside the light one.
Docs: https://developer.mozilla.org/docs/Web/HTML/Element/meta/name/theme-color#media
Done when: `spiderlint audit ORIGIN/ --rules html/theme-color-schemes` reports no html/theme-color-schemes finding, and `spiderlint facts ORIGIN/about` shows `html.metas` meeting it.

